ou  cope with the shock of losing your job  it can help cope with the anxiety of the  implications of what that might mean in  your life and to your family  and it can help rebuild confidence and  sort of finding a  clear sense of purpose as you go back  out and look for work so it's more about  how do we build up our inner resilience  to cope with what's going on in our life  rather than necessarily sort of changing  what's happening in our life  no andy there are people out there and  they're people watching right now they  probably just tried to leave the room  come back this question's for you  uh who think i'm just not the kind of  person who meditates i'm not a  meditation type person  what do you say to that individual in  particular  i would say that as human beings we  share many things and  one of we all struggle with our mind at  times and we all need a way to cope  with those struggles meditation is a  scientifically proven way  of coping with those struggles so even  if you think this isn't something for  you i always say to people  if you think it's not for you experiment  prove to yourself that it's not for you  try it  for five minutes a day for ten days and  see if it makes a difference or not  if you get to the end of the 10 days  it's made no difference okay you've  proven yourself that you're right  but maybe you might be surprised we  often see that the benefits of  meditation  although it's not a quick fix the  benefits of meditation have felt very  very early on  and the science suggests that it's less  about duration and how long we sit for  and it's more about frequency  so showing up for just a few minutes a  day can make a really big difference  well then if people who want to start  what should they know about showing up  to meditate that first time what should  their expectations be how do they get  started  yeah so look i i think there's three  things that spring to mind the first one  is  think of this a little bit like physical  exerc